= turbo_stream.update("modal-frame") do
  -#
    The backend failure path (`new` rescuing DcommsClient::Error) has no `@entry` to name,
    so the subtitle falls back to the dialog title alone rather than raising on the way to
    the error the user needs to see. The error itself is rendered inside the dialog by the
    form partial, which renders it whether or not the entry was looked up.
  = v.modal(t("app_installs.title"), subtitle: @entry&.name, size: "md", close_button: true) do |modal|
    = turbo_frame_tag "install-dialog" do
      = render "form", modal: modal
